  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe active-client test now queues each next complete ping before it releases the current owner reply. Client scheduling after a reply cannot create an unintended idle period. The test checks eight successful JSON replies over at least two idle windows. The same connection must then receive an idle notice and EOF when messages stop.\n\nOnly the test and its decision note changed. The listener, hello deadline, security rules, idle configuration, and existing negative tests did not change.\n\n## Before and after\n\nBaseline: `751a79b20327fa73743f032f2f3d99907334cbe3`.\n\nThe old test slept for 150 ms between replies and requests with a 400 ms idle window. A temporary Linux probe added a 300 ms scheduling delay after each reply. The old test failed with `BrokenPipe`. The synchronized test passed with the same delay and the original 400 ms window. This demonstrates the synchronization correction separately from the final scheduling allowance.\n\nThe final test uses a two-second idle window. Each owner reply waits for one quarter of that window. The elapsed assertion requires at least two windows of activity. Socket waits and request waits have a finite limit of three windows.\n\nTwo temporary negative controls confirmed the assertions:\n- Removing the complete-message activity refresh failed during active replies with `ConnectionReset`.\n- Disabling idle expiry failed at the final idle-notice read with `WouldBlock`.\n\nBoth mutations and all probe delays were removed before the final checks.\n\n## Checks on `3f6a6c5e8950505e3caf29035a42c41749066856`\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: passed the complete `mcp_live` suite, 29 tests. This includes `a_client_that_keeps_talking_is_never_dropped_as_idle`, silent-client expiry, slow-loris expiry, idle configuration, and hello/security tests.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --only 'motion light:' --only 'app light:'`: passed all 11 light tests in five test steps. The broad build-only step was omitted; each selected test target compiled and ran.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- The changed test function matches `rustfmt` output for edition 2024. `git diff --check` passed.\n\nAll checks used Linux and three jobs. Windows reproduction, Windows gates, full heavy lanes, release packaging, and machinery were not exercised. No post or toolpath changed, so catalog regeneration does not apply.\n\n## Readings and decisions\n\nRead the full issue thread, the current listener, the active-client test, and the idle-configuration tests. Decision: `docs/decisions/3230-live-idle-test.md`.\n\nNo scout was supplied. Direct reads covered those exact files, `crates/app/src/clock.rs`, the decision format, and current process skills. Direct Git history covered `crates/app/tests/mcp_live.rs`. Fresh complete open-PR file inventories found no overlapping changed path and no release branch PR.\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3230#issuecomment-7224215735\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3230\n",
